    "body": "# Stanford — MS\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#1 (tie) in U.S. News Best Computer Science Schools · graduate departments, April 2026 release.\n\n33 departments occupy ranks 1–27. All seven schools tied at 27 are included. This is a graduate department ranking, not a ranking of the specific master’s routes listed here.\n\nRanking provenance: [IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/). The publisher’s direct table was inaccessible; the position is secondary-source reported.\n\nUniversity: Stanford University\n\nDegree route: MS in Computer Science\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\n45-unit master’s with coursework or research options; MS admission does not guarantee entry to the PhD. Application open: 15 Sep 2026 (deadline research 2026-10-20; see deadline field).\n\nOrientation: Coursework or research · 45 units\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$69,717 — Academic-year tuition (Engineering, 11–18 units × 3 quarters); 2026–27.\n\n2026–27 reference, not a Fall 2027 quote or full-degree total.\n\nGraduate School of Engineering quarterly rate for 11–18 units is $23,239 (2026–27). Three academic-year quarters (Autumn–Spring) = $69,717. 8–10 units is $15,100/quarter. Per-unit above 18: $1,549. MS CS requires 45 units; HCP/online uses a different per-unit schedule. Living costs and Cardinal Care are separate.\n\nApplication timing: Apps open 15 Sep 2026 · Deadline 8 Dec 2026 · 11:59 p.m. PT (Autumn / Fall 2027 entry). Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nCS MS pages and Stanford Grad Aid: no guaranteed department funding for MS; international students generally ineligible for Stanford/federal loans. Course/Research Assistant roles exist but are limited; PhD priority. Knight-Hennessy (SCH-002) listed in catalog but 2027 application closed.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-002. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Master's admissions](https://www.cs.stanford.edu/admissions/masters-admissions)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://studentservices.stanford.edu/tuition-rates/2026-2027-graduate-and-professional-tuition-rates)\n- [MS requirements](https://www.cs.stanford.edu/masters-degree-requirements)\n- [Specializations](https://www.cs.stanford.edu/masters-specializations)\n- [The Student Budget (graduate)](https://financialaid.stanford.edu/grad/budget/)\n- [Estimate Your Graduate Charges](https://studentservices.stanford.edu/my-finances/tuition-fees/estimate-your-graduate-charges-0)\n- [CS MS CA/RA overview](https://www.cs.stanford.edu/masters-course-assistant-and-research-assistant)\n- [CS graduate application deadlines](https://www.cs.stanford.edu/admissions-graduate-application-deadlines)\n- [Stanford Grad Admissions apply (11:59 p.m. Pacific Time)](https://gradadmissions.stanford.edu/apply/apply-now)\n- [U.S. News positions via IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
