    "body": "# Virginia Darden — MBA\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#11 (tie) in U.S. News Best Business Schools · full-time MBA, April 2026 release.\n\n30 schools occupy ranks 1–29; ties are retained. These are full-time MBA ranks, not business subject, online MBA or specialized master’s ranks.\n\nRanking provenance: [Clear Admit](https://www.clearadmit.com/mba-rankings/usnews/). The publisher’s direct table was inaccessible; the position is secondary-source reported.\n\nUniversity: University of Virginia\n\nDegree route: Full-Time MBA\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nFull-time MBA academic route; curriculum and experiential-learning details are linked for deeper comparison.\n\nOrientation: Full-time MBA · Management\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$83,328 — Academic-year tuition (Darden MBA, Non-Virginia domicile); 2026–27.\n\n2026–27 reference, not a Fall 2027 quote or full-degree total.\n\nDarden Tuition, Fees & Billing for Class of 2028: Fall 2026 / Spring 2027 Tuition $41,664 per semester for Non-Virginia domicile and International students → $83,328 AY. Virginia domicile tuition $39,505/semester → $79,010 AY. Comprehensive and activity fees are separate; published Fall/Spring Tuition & Fees (excl. case fees) are $44,000 Non-VA / $41,500 VA per semester ($88,000 / $83,000 AY). COA Class of 2028 lists Tuition & Fees $88,000 Non-VA / $88,240 International / $83,000 Virginia, plus case fees $1,100. Health insurance $4,220 billed in Fall if on UVA plan. Full-time residential MBA — not EMBA.\n\nApplication timing: Round 2 · 7 Jan 2027 (Full-Time MBA Class of 2029 / Aug 2027; EA & R1 passed; clock time not on table). Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nMaster’s scholarship eligibility, award coverage and deadlines are not yet verified. Doctoral funding must not be assumed to cover this degree.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: No verified award links yet. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [MBA academics](https://www.darden.virginia.edu/mba/academics)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://www.darden.virginia.edu/mba/tuition-financial-aid/tuition-fees-billing)\n- [Cost of Attendance](https://www.darden.virginia.edu/mba/tuition-financial-aid/cost-of-attendance)\n- [MBA Apply Deadlines (2026–27 / Class of 2029)](https://www.darden.virginia.edu/mba/admissions/apply/deadlines)\n- [Darden 2026–27 Full-Time MBA Application Live](https://www.darden.virginia.edu/programs/blog/2026-27-full-time-mba-application-live)\n- [MBA program](https://www.darden.virginia.edu/mba/)\n- [U.S. News positions via Clear Admit](https://www.clearadmit.com/mba-rankings/usnews/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
